<!-- ll-message demo — mirrors the upstream docs page (#/components/message):
     intro, then the Examples entries with the page's own copy. -->
<view class="demo">
  <view class="demo-title">Message</view>
  <view class="sec-desc">The row of a chat message: an avatar, a column with a header, the bubbles and a footer, aligned to the start or the end. Also MessageText, which sets a reply word by word so streaming text soaks in like wet ink.</view>

  <view class="sec">
    <view class="sec-h2">Examples</view>

    <view class="sub-h3">A thread</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">Two speakers. The footer of the first message rides above the avatar, so the avatar keeps standing beside the last bubble.</view>
    <view class="ms-col">
      <ll-message align="end">
        <ll-message-content>
          <ll-message-header>Ada</ll-message-header>
          <ll-bubble variant="default">
            <ll-bubble-content seed="thread-1">Which of these should I fix first?</ll-bubble-content>
          </ll-bubble>
        </ll-message-content>
      </ll-message>
      <ll-message>
        <ll-message-avatar><ll-mascot pose="write" size="{{40}}" seed="thread-mascot" /></ll-message-avatar>
        <ll-message-content>
          <ll-message-header>Stubby</ll-message-header>
          <ll-bubble-group>
            <ll-bubble variant="muted">
              <ll-bubble-content seed="thread-2">The failing test. Everything else can wait until it is green.</ll-bubble-content>
            </ll-bubble>
            <ll-bubble variant="muted">
              <ll-bubble-content seed="thread-3">It is a one-line fix in filter.ts.</ll-bubble-content>
            </ll-bubble>
          </ll-bubble-group>
          <ll-message-footer>edited a minute ago</ll-message-footer>
        </ll-message-content>
      </ll-message>
    </view>

    <view class="sub-h3">Streaming text</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">MessageText keeps the words already on the page and soaks each new word in as it arrives: dark and blurred at first, then dry. A felt-tip caret rides after the last word.</view>
    <view class="ms-col">
      <ll-message>
        <ll-message-content>
          <ll-message-header>Stubby</ll-message-header>
          <ll-bubble variant="muted" custom-style="max-width:100%;">
            <ll-bubble-content seed="stream">
              <ll-message-text text="{{streamText}}" streaming="{{streaming}}" seed="stream-words" />
              <text wx:if="{{count === 0}}" class="dots">...</text>
            </ll-bubble-content>
          </ll-bubble>
        </ll-message-content>
      </ll-message>
      <view class="row"><ll-button size="sm" variant="ghost" bind:tap="replay">Replay</ll-button></view>
    </view>

    <view class="sub-h3">In your own hand</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">pen="you" sets a bubble in blue felt and the script face. MessageText keeps its words plain inline text with a baseline offset and a lighter ink, so the tall last letters of a script face (d, l, e, !) are whole.</view>
    <view class="ms-col">
      <ll-message align="end">
        <ll-message-content>
          <ll-message-header>you</ll-message-header>
          <ll-bubble variant="tinted" pen="you">
            <ll-bubble-content seed="hand-1">
              <ll-message-text text="Call me when the old road is closed, and bring the good umbrella!" seed="hand-words-1" />
            </ll-bubble-content>
          </ll-bubble>
        </ll-message-content>
      </ll-message>
      <ll-message>
        <ll-message-avatar><ll-mascot pose="write" size="{{40}}" seed="hand-mascot" /></ll-message-avatar>
        <ll-message-content>
          <ll-message-header>Stubby</ll-message-header>
          <ll-bubble variant="muted">
            <ll-bubble-content seed="hand-2">
              <ll-message-text text="Noted. I will call at six and read you the whole plan aloud." seed="hand-words-2" />
            </ll-bubble-content>
          </ll-bubble>
        </ll-message-content>
      </ll-message>
    </view>
  </view>
</view>
